    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d173">

                <pb facs="0415" n="389" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v09/pg389"/>

                <head>173. Letter From the Under Secretary of State (Ball) to Secretary of the
                    Treasury Dillon<anchor n="0" xml:id="d173-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1963-08-23">August 23,
                        1963</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Doug</hi>: In connection with your letter of
                    July 24,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d173-f2"/> I believe you will find the
                    Department’s reply to Secretary McNamara’s letter of July 9,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d173-f3"/> which is attached for your information, useful in
                    explaining our views on the promotion of military sales.</p>
                <p>To ensure that the objectives desired by the President are fully understood by
                    posts abroad where this policy is to be applied, we are in the process of
                    coordinating with AID and Defense a circular instruction to <pb facs="0416"
                        n="390" xml:id="pg390"/> the field. I will be pleased to forward a copy of
                    it to you when it is ready for transmittal.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d173-f4"/></p>
                <p>With warm personal regards,</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">George</hi><anchor n="4" xml:id="d173-f5"
                        /></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d173-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d173-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, DEF 19-3. Confidential. Forwarded to
                    Under Secretary Ball for his signature under cover of an August 5 memorandum
                    from U. Alexis Johnson to Ball. The August 23 date was later stamped on the
                    source text when it was sent to Secretary Dillon.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d173-f2" n="1" xml:id="d173-f2-content">
                <p>In this letter to Secretary Rusk, also attached to the source text and Johnson’s
                    memorandum, Dillon advised that the Department should send a circular containing
                    the key paragraphs of NSAM No. 242 to the attention of some Country Teams abroad
                    (including some MAAGs) because these teams could provide the “most direct help,
                    both to the governments to which they are accredited and to U.S. defense
                    industry representatives, in promoting sales opportunities.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d173-f3" n="2" xml:id="d173-f3-content">
                <p><ref target="#d170">Documents 170</ref> and <ref target="#d171">171</ref>. A copy
                    of the Secretary’s July 26 letter to McNamara is also attached to the source
                    text.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d173-f4" n="3" xml:id="d173-f4-content">
                <p>Text in CA-2258, August 26; see the Supplement.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d173-f5" n="4" xml:id="d173-f5-content">
                <p>Printed from a copy that indicates Ball signed the original.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
